  m_Name: BalanceMachine
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GravityBox.Gameplay::GravityBox.Gameplay.LevelDefinition
  Id: steel-lab-balancemachine
  DisplayIndex: 18
  DisplayName: Two balls, one balance
  Shape: 17
  TeachingHint: A has the longer lever arm. Lift B, seat the catch, then free BOTH
    balls.
  Environment: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 82e0ce24addfe4fc89b8bbd0db998aea, type: 2}
  Prefab: {fileID: 3791338402302016940, guid: 33314633e1f8542d8b630f0b51b1f63d, type: 3}
  RotationMode: 1
  InitialLocalVelocity: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  ParSeconds: 0
  Tutorial: 0
  DesignerSolution: Two equal steel balls load different lever arms. The far ball
    supplies the torque that raises the near ball and aligns its lane with the receiving
    ledge. A contact-operated catch retains the seated lever, allowing both balls
    to leave their lanes and reach the round exit. No powered lift or identity-specific
    ball forces. Shared exit assist pulls the ball through an unobstructed opening
    within 40 mm. This is deliberate gameplay assistance; the entire sphere must
    still physically clear the bore before completion.
